      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find \\(\\cos 150^\\circ\\), we can use the cosine addition formula. First, recognize that \\(150^\\circ\\) can be expressed as \\(180^\\circ - 30^\\circ\\). This gives us:\n\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = \\cos (180^\\circ - 30^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nUsing the cosine subtraction formula, \\(\\cos (180^\\circ - \\theta) = -\\cos \\theta\\), we substitute \\(\\theta = 30^\\circ\\):\n\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = -\\cos 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\(\\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\). Therefore:\n\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\n\\]",
